<!--
  SwipeDelete Zero — primary mark. CONCEPT 1: "the negative".

  A single frame of film negative. Sprocket notches bite into the left and
  right edges; the frame's aperture is cut clean through as a "0".

  The whole mark is one path with evenOdd fill, so it is a true silhouette:
  it works in one flat colour, inverts cleanly, and needs no strokes — which
  is what keeps it readable at 16px where stroked marks collapse.

  Geometry (48dp viewport, all values exact):
    frame    x 4..44, y 4..44, corner r 7.5
    notches  r 4, centred ON the edge at y 18 and y 30, both sides
    zero     ellipse at (24,24), rx 9, ry 11.5  (taller than wide, as a 0 is)
-->
